dt-bindings: iommu: rockchip: describe the RK3576 NPU MMU

The binding allows two register ranges, two clocks and one power domain,
which every Rockchip IOMMU satisfied until the RK3576 NPU MMU. That one
has four ranges - a pair per NPU core - with each pair inside its own
core's power domain, and the extra clocks those banks and the command
buffer need. dtc accepts the node as written; dtbs_check does not.

Give it its own compatible rather than widening rockchip,rk3576-iommu,
which the two-bank VOP MMU on the same SoC also uses. The NPU MMU is then
constrained to exactly four ranges, five clocks and two domains, and
everything else keeps the original limits.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
       - items:
           - enum:
               - rockchip,rk3576-iommu
+              - rockchip,rk3576-npu-iommu
               - rockchip,rk3588-iommu
           - const: rockchip,rk3568-iommu
 
@@ -33,6 +34,8 @@
     items:
       - description: configuration registers for MMU instance 0
       - description: configuration registers for MMU instance 1
+      - description: configuration registers for MMU instance 2
+      - description: configuration registers for MMU instance 3
     minItems: 1
 
   interrupts:
@@ -45,17 +48,26 @@
     items:
       - description: Core clock
       - description: Interface clock
+      - description: Core clock for the second bank pair
+      - description: Command buffer core clock
+      - description: Command buffer interface clock
+    minItems: 2
 
   clock-names:
     items:
       - const: aclk
       - const: iface
+      - const: aclk1
+      - const: aclk_cbuf
+      - const: hclk_cbuf
+    minItems: 2
 
   "#iommu-cells":
     const: 0
 
   power-domains:
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 2
 
   rockchip,disable-mmu-reset:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
@@ -64,6 +76,44 @@
       Some mmu instances may produce unexpected results
       when the reset operation is used.
 
+allOf:
+  # The RK3576 NPU MMU is the only one with more than one bank pair: four
+  # register ranges, a pair per NPU core, each pair in that core's own power
+  # domain, with the extra clocks those banks and the command buffer need.
+  # Everything else, including the two-bank RK3576 VOP MMU, keeps the original
+  # limits.
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: rockchip,rk3576-npu-iommu
+    then:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          minItems: 4
+          maxItems: 4
+        clocks:
+          minItems: 5
+          maxItems: 5
+        clock-names:
+          minItems: 5
+          maxItems: 5
+        power-domains:
+          minItems: 2
+          maxItems: 2
+      required:
+        - power-domains
+    else:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          maxItems: 2
+        clocks:
+          maxItems: 2
+        clock-names:
+          maxItems: 2
+        power-domains:
+          maxItems: 1
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
